    "body": "\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFix Gemma4 engine crash / silent accuracy drop when encoder CUDA graph is on.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n1. Fix engine crash when `max_soft_tokens` is not the default. In `prepare_encoder_cudagraph_capture_inputs` the launch-time option `mm_processor_kwargs.max_soft_tokens` is ignored, thus serving an image fails with a shape-mismatch `RuntimeError` in `pad_pixel_values` at graph replay.\r\n2. ~~Fix wrong embeddings when the replay stride differs from the capture stride. Before the fix, capture stride depends on `max_soft_tokens` but replay stride is a fixed 70. Thus Frame 2 onwards in a video can read the wrong rows.~~ Fixed in #61365 \r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nLaunch a Gemma4 server with encoder CUDA graph on and non-default `max_soft_tokens`, and send a vision question.\r\n\r\n```shell\r\n# set max vision items per batch to 16 to avoid OOM\r\nvllm serve google/gemma-4-E2B-it \\\r\n  --mm-processor-kwargs.max_soft_tokens 560 \\\r\n  --compilation-config.cudagraph_mm_encoder true \\\r\n  --compilation-config.encoder_cudagraph_max_vision_items_per_batch 16\r\n```\r\n\r\nOn main:\r\n\r\n```log\r\n...\r\n(Worker_DP6_EP6 pid=6328) ERROR 10-07 05:27:08 [multiproc_executor.py:1058]   File \"/app/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/v1/worker/encoder_cudagraph.py\", line 451, in _run_budget_graph\r\n(Worker_DP6_EP6 pid=6328) ERROR 10-07 05:27:08 [multiproc_executor.py:1058]     padding_logic(buf, src)\r\n(Worker_DP6_EP6 pid=6328) ERROR 10-07 05:27:08 [multiproc_executor.py:1058]   File \"/app/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/model_executor/models/gemma4_mm.py\", line 1652, in pad_pixel_values\r\n(Worker_DP6_EP6 pid=6328) ERROR 10-07 05:27:08 [multiproc_executor.py:1058]     dst[:batch_size, :num_patches].copy_(src)\r\n(Worker_DP6_EP6 pid=6328) ERROR 10-07 05:27:08 [multiproc_executor.py:1058] RuntimeError: The size of tensor a (2520) must match the size of tensor b (5040) at non-singleton dimension 1\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis PR:\r\n\r\nNo crash\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\nEncoder CUDA graph on Gemma4 is already working well on upstream main when `max_soft_tokens` is not set. This PR is for non-default `max_soft_tokens`.\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [ ] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
